    {
      "practice": "CSMs ask customers who scored 9 or 10 on the last NPS survey to review us on G2.",
      "problem": "Review gating: only promoters are invited. G2 bans collection that leaves out likely negative reviews, and the FTC says gating can break Section 5 of the FTC Act.",
      "fix": "Invite all 860 contacts who meet the neutral review rule, with one message. Accounts with low scores or open escalations (here 3 named) are invited too; their issues go to CS separately."
    },
    {
      "practice": "We send a 25 USD gift card to customers who leave a 5-star review on G2.",
      "problem": "The reward depends on a 5-star rating. G2 and the FTC rule on reviews (16 CFR Part 465) ban incentives tied to what the review says.",
      "fix": "Stop it now. Use the G2 decision below or no reward."
    }
  ],
  "practice_notes": [
    {
      "practice": "Account managers ask for references from whoever they know best.",
      "finding": "Not a rule breach, but it is why Fitness account A107 took 3 reference calls in 51 days. The ask budget in this plan replaces it."
    }
